.SH DESCRIPTION
The kernel walks the PCI buses at boot and keeps a
.B Pcidev
for each function: its
.B tbdf
(bus type, bus, device and function, printed by
.LR %T ),
vendor and device ids, class, the base address registers it was given
.RB ( mem [ i ] .bar
and
.BR .size ),
interrupt line, latency, cache line size, its command register
.RB ( pcr ),
and the bridges above and below it
.RB ( parent ,
.BR bridge ).
That record is the host's configuration of the function: what it
should have whenever the host is using it.
.PP
.I Pcimatch
returns the function after
.I prev
(from the start if
.I prev
is nil) whose vendor and device ids match, zero matching any;
.I pcimatchtbdf
the one at
.IR tbdf .
.IR Pcicfgr8 ,
.IR pcicfgr16 ,
.I pcicfgr32
and the matching writes read and write its configuration space.
.I Pcicap
and
.I pciextcap
give the offset of a capability, or of an extended (PCI Express)
capability, or \-1.
.PP
.I Pcienable
powers a function to D0 (and its bridges first), turns on the
decoders its BARs need, and, coming back from D3, puts back the
configuration in its
.BR Pcidev .
.I Pcidisable
turns off its MSI and MSI-X and its bus mastering;
.I pcisetbme
and
.I pciclrbme
turn bus mastering on and off, keeping
.B pcr
in step.
.I Pcisetpms
sets its power state, returning the old one, or \-1.
.PP
.I Pcimsixcount
gives the number of MSI-X vectors a function has.
.I Pcimsixintrenable
(nil where the platform cannot deliver MSI-X) gives vector
.I vec
a host interrupt vector, points the table entry at it and unmasks it,
calling
.I f
with
.I a
on each interrupt, like
.IR intrenable (10);
.I pcimsixintrdisable
undoes it, and
.I pcimsixmask
masks or unmasks the entry.
.PP
Three functions reset one function without a driver's help, each
putting back afterwards the configuration in its
.B Pcidev
(BARs, interrupt line, latency, cache line, then the command
register) and each returning zero where it cannot be done.  The
caller has stopped the function first
.RI ( pcidisable ).
.I Pciflr
does a function-level reset (PCI Express base specification 6.6.2)
where its PCI Express capability offers one: it waits up to 100 ms for
transactions pending, starts the reset, and waits the 100 ms the
specification allows.
.I Pcisbr
has the bridge above it do a secondary bus reset, only where the
function is all there is below that bridge: the reset held 2 ms, then
100 ms to come back.
.I Pcifnreset
tries the first, then the second, and says which it did
.RB ( FLR
or
.BR "secondary bus reset" ),
or returns nil.
.IR Vm (3)
uses it to reset a function a machine had when the machine ends.
.PP
.I Pcisriov
reads a physical function's SR-IOV capability into
.IR s ;
.I pcisriovenable
makes
.I n
virtual functions (0 removes them), which then appear as functions of
their own (the hook
.B pcidevadded
is called for each, which
.IR iommu (3)
uses to put them in its host domain), returning nil or an error string.
